docs/ADOPTION.ja.md:537:| audit open が exit 6 / `config-change-unaccepted` | 前 run が config 変更を検知 | `git diff .claude/doc-audit.json` を確認し、承認後に `/docaudit:audit --accept-config` |
docs/ADOPTION.md:306:| `impactMap` | object[] | yes | `{changed: path\|glob, impacts: [docPath,…], note?: string, source?: string}` — the heart (see §6). `source:"audit-scope"` is generated. May start empty `[]`. |
docs/ADOPTION.md:338:### When `audit-scope.json` exists
docs/ADOPTION.md:340:`audit-scope.json` is the source of truth; `impactMap` entries marked `source:"audit-scope"` are generated output. Phase 0 stops on drift. Restore it with `/docaudit:init --import-audit-scope`. Importing between runs does not need `--accept-config`; exit 6 applies only when an active run refuses a config change. An active run lock rejects imports. `{"impact":"none"}` suppresses generated mapping, but the heuristic can still select that document.
docs/ADOPTION.md:467:- The gate has additional **REFUSED** conditions for provenance/audit-scope integrity and strict
docs/ADOPTION.md:482:This mirrors a real onboarding. Expect the first `--full` to find genuine drift — that's the
